# p5/payload/filemap -- THE payload declaration. scripts/build-p5-package.sh
# copies this file verbatim to <package>/payload/filemap, and p5-install reads
# it there (p5/bin/p5-install:265-285).
#
# FORMAT, exactly as p5-install parses it: mode|role|src|dest
#   mode  octal file mode, passed to `install -m`
#   role  client | server | both -- a row whose role is neither `both` nor the
#         installing box's role is SKIPPED, which is what makes one package
#         serve both boxes without either being a special case
#   src   path relative to the package's payload/ dir. It is the REPO path of
#         the file (ADR-005 section 4: source paths do not change), or a build/
#         path for something the builder produces rather than copies
#   dest  absolute production destination, from ADR-005 section 4's map
#
# NO PADDING SPACES. p5-install splits on `|` with a raw `read` and does not
# trim, so a column aligned with spaces becomes a mode/role/dest that carries
# them.
#
# EVERY DEST HERE IS A DECLARED ROW IN p5/contract/paths, and p5-install
# re-checks each one against contract/foreign, contract/namespace and
# contract/paths at install time (p5_check_dest, p5-common.sh:658). A dest that
# is not declared there is refused with exit 4 -- so this file cannot widen the
# namespace, only fill it.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE, each with its reason:
#   /etc/hotplug.d/iface/[0-9][0-9]-p5  contract/paths:159 leaves the two-digit
#       priority UNSET on purpose -- choosing it is choosing an ordering against
#       netifd's other hooks, which is E5's derivation to make and justify
#       (CONTRACT.md:344-346). deploy/p5/97-bond therefore has no destination
#       yet and is not shipped.
#   /etc/config/p5                      contract/paths:160 is conditional on a
#       decision E5 has not made.
#   deploy/p5/shape-install, deploy/p5/init.d/cake-autorate, deploy/p5/portal/*,
#   deploy/p5/shape/*                   no row in contract/paths declares a
#       destination for them, so p5-install would refuse them with exit 4.
#       They are shipped when a contract row exists, not before.
#
# ARCHITECTURE. The two Go binaries are built GOOS=linux GOARCH=arm64: both
# boxes are aarch64 (.github/workflows/emulator-gate.yml:271-273 for the
# GL-MT2500 server, :738 for the client). CONTRACT.md:348-350 says the
# architecture choice is U28's and is expressed as filemap rows -- these two
# rows are that expression.
#
# mode|role|src|dest

# ---- the datapath: the client daemon and its procd service ----------------
755|client|build/linux-arm64/p5-datapath|/usr/sbin/p5-datapath
755|client|deploy/p5/init.d/bond-agg|/etc/init.d/p5-datapath

# ---- the server daemon and its procd service ------------------------------
# contract/paths:158 (/etc/init.d/p5-server) is an E5-RESERVED row, and reserved
# is not a bar: p5_check_dest admits it exactly as it admits the other reserved
# rows shipped above (/etc/init.d/p5-datapath, /usr/sbin/p5). The source is
# deploy/server/init.d/p5-server, whose own header (:4-6) names that dest and
# that contract row. Without this row --role server would place a daemon with no
# service and docs/deploy-p5-server.md:431 S3 would keep delivering it by hand.
755|server|build/linux-arm64/p5-server|/usr/sbin/p5-server
755|server|deploy/server/init.d/p5-server|/etc/init.d/p5-server

# ---- the client control plane --------------------------------------------
755|client|deploy/p5/bondctl|/usr/sbin/p5
755|client|deploy/p5/bond-xctl|/usr/sbin/p5-reconciler
755|client|deploy/p5/bond-ecod|/usr/sbin/p5-ecod
755|client|deploy/p5/bond-watchdog|/usr/sbin/p5-watchdog
755|client|deploy/p5/init.d/bond-ecod|/etc/init.d/p5-ecod
755|client|deploy/p5/init.d/bond-watchdog|/etc/init.d/p5-watchdog

# ---- product data: read-only, version-locked, NOT configuration ----------
644|client|deploy/p5/bond.dag|/usr/lib/p5/dag
644|client|deploy/p5/lib/xctl-lock.sh|/usr/lib/p5/xctl-lock.sh
644|client|deploy/p5/lib/xctl-probe.sh|/usr/lib/p5/xctl-probe.sh
644|client|deploy/p5/lib/xctl-actions.sh|/usr/lib/p5/xctl-actions.sh
644|client|deploy/p5/lib/xctl-shape.sh|/usr/lib/p5/xctl-shape.sh
644|client|deploy/p5/lib/xctl-dag.sh|/usr/lib/p5/xctl-dag.sh
